# Ozma node — hardware profile
# Install as /etc/ozma/ozma-node-hardware.env (system unit) or copy beside a
# user unit. EnvironmentFile syntax: KEY=VALUE, no shell expansion.
#
# The unit passes --profile hardware explicitly. OZMA_NODE_ARGS is split at
# whitespace by systemd and is the place for flags without an OZMA_* variable
# (for example --hls, --display-output, or --usb-gadget).

OZMA_CAPTURE_DEVICE=/dev/video0
# Optional: advertise/publish the camera node's audio sink.
# OZMA_AUDIO_SINK=ozma-hw

# Local HLS is opt-in; set OZMA_NODE_ARGS below to enable it. The path must be
# writable by the service user (ReadWritePaths in the unit).
OZMA_HLS_DIR=/var/lib/ozma-node/hls
OZMA_NODE_ARGS=--hls --hls-fps 30

# Bind to loopback for the browser WebTransport listener unless a reverse
# proxy terminates TLS for the LAN.
OZMA_WEBTRANSPORT_BIND=127.0.0.1
# OZMA_WEBTRANSPORT_PORT=4433
# OZMA_API_TOKEN=replace-with-a-secret   # keep the file mode 0600

RUST_LOG=ozma_node=info,ozma_capture=info
